    "https://facultypositions.stanford.edu/jobs/open-rank-faculty-position-in-smart-manufacturing-stanford-university-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Position in Smart Manufacturing",
      "description": "Open Rank Faculty Position in Smart Manufacturing - Stanford University, California, United States Stanford Faculty Positions Site navigation Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode Open Faculty Positions Open Rank Faculty Position in Smart Manufacturing Stanford University University Tenure Line Opening at: Oct 2 2026 - 9:00am PDT Closing at: Oct 1 2027 - 11:55pm PDT Add to favorites View favorites The School of Engineering ( https://engineering.stanford.edu/ ) at Stanford University invites applicants for an all-ranks faculty search in the area of Smart Manufacturing. The appointment will be at the tenure-track assistant professor, tenure-track or tenured associate professor, or tenured full professor rank. The primary home department will be one of the nine departments in the School of Engineering ( https://engineering.stanford.edu/faculty-research/departments ) and will be determined during the search process. Manufacturing is being transformed by the convergence of advances in sensing, autonomy, materials science, data infrastructure, artificial intelligence, optimization, and human-machine collaboration. These technologies are reshaping how physical products are designed, produced, monitored, and improved, blurring the boundary between the digital and physical worlds. This shift is enabling new levels of automation, adaptability, and sustainability across the manufacturing lifecycle from individual unit processes to entire supply networks, creating rich opportunities for cross-disciplinary collaboration across engineering and beyond. We invite applications from individuals pursuing research in Smart Manufacturing, broadly defined to include topics such as advanced and additive manufacturing, in-situ sensing and closed-loop process control, AI-driven design and defect detection, digital twins, robotics and automation, cyber-physical production systems, industrialized construction, sustainable and circular manufacturing, and data-driven operations and supply chains. Candidates can be conducting this work in the context of any engineering discipline. Successful candidates should be conducting world-class research and translating their results into real-world impact in their domain (or, for junior candidates, have demonstrated potential to do so). In addition to excellence in research, we expect candidates to be or become educational leaders in advanced manufacturing topics and to effectively communicate the role of advanced and smart technologies in shaping the future of manufacturing, including considering its broader societal impacts. Applicants must have completed, or be completing, a Ph.D. in the advertised field or a closely related one. Evidence of the ability to pursue a program of research, and a strong commitment to graduate and undergraduate teaching are also required. A successful candidate will be expected to teach courses at the graduate and undergraduate levels and to build and lead a team of graduate students in Ph.D. research. The School of Engineering and Stanford University value faculty who will help foster an open and respectful academic environment for colleagues, students, and staff with a wide range of backgrounds and perspectives. Candidates may choose to include as part of their research and teaching statements a brief discussion about how their work and experience further these values. Applications should include the following materials: Cover letter CV Brief statements of research and teaching interests (3-5 pages total for both combined).  Candidates are encouraged to describe not only their accomplishments but also specific planned research projects and courses that they might like to teach. Two representative publications Names and e-mail addresses of 3-5 references. If a candidate currently holds a tenured faculty appointment, their references will only be contacted if they are short-listed. For all other applicants, references will be contacted immediately upon the submission of the application. In the cover letter, applicants should identify potential home department(s) in the School of Engineering. In addition to applying to this search, if a potential home department has an active search at their rank, applicants should also apply to the departmental search and indicate in that application that they have also applied to the Smart Manufacturing search. Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026. If you have questions regarding this opening or require assistance with the online application system, please contact the Faculty Search Administrator at soefacultysearch@stanford.edu . The expected base pay range for this position is: Assistant Professor: $144,100- $163,766 Associate Professor (untenured): $158,510 - $196,803 Associate Professor (tenured): $168,510 - $206,803 Professor: $180,000 - $271,748 This base pay range is for a nine-month academic appointment and does not include summer salary.  For more information about compensation and our wide range of benefits, including housing assistance, please contact the hiring department. Stanford University has provided a pay range representing its good faith estimate of what the university reasonably expects to pay for the position upon hire. The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors including (but not limited to) the experience and qualifications of the selected candidate including years since terminal degree, training, and field or discipline; departmental budget availability; internal equity; and external market pay for comparable jobs. Stanford is an equal employment opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Stanford welcomes applications from all who would bring additional dimensions to the University’s research, teaching and clinical missions. Consistent with its obligations under the law, the University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities. Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact disability.access@stanford.edu . Back to all jobs Apply Now First Name (required) 110c0fda Last Name (required) 0d7b379d Email (required) 05967a9f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 8f08dfc8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. School School of Engineering School of Engineering Line University Tenure Line University Tenure Line Location Stanford University, California, United States Stanford University, California, United States First Name (required) 160bc3fd Last Name (required) daf24f39 Email (required) 5e7db1ca Subscribe Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Get Help Questions about a job or your application? Find out how to request help Equal Opportunity Stanford is an equal employment opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Stanford welcomes applications from all who would bring additional dimensions to the University’s research, teaching and clinical missions. Consistent with its obligations under the law, the University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities. Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact disability.access@stanford.edu . Stanford University Stanford Home Maps & Directions Search Stanford Emergency Info Terms of Use Cookie Preferences Privacy Copyright Trademarks Non-Discrimination Accessibility © 2026 Stanford University. Stanford, California 94305. Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://facultypositions.stanford.edu/jobs/clinical-assistant-professor-stanford-dermatology-stanford-university-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Stanford Dermatology",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor, Stanford Dermatology - Stanford University, California, United States Stanford Faculty Positions Site navigation Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode Open Faculty Positions Clinical Assistant Professor, Stanford Dermatology Stanford University CE - Clinician Educator Opening at: Aug 20 2026 - 9:00am PDT Closing at: Jan 31 2027 - 11:55pm PST Add to favorites View favorites The Department of Dermatology at Stanford University School of Medicine is seeking board-certified or board-eligible dermatologists to join the faculty as Clinical Assistant Professors in the Clinician Educator line. This is a full-time, non-tenure eligible academic appointment, offering the opportunity to provide outstanding dermatologic care with a strong commitment to teaching and mentoring trainees and medical students. We are seeking candidates with an MD or MD/PhD who are interested in developing a clinical practice that aligns with departmental needs and individual expertise. The major criteria for appointment for Clinician Educators is excellence in the overall mix of clinical care, teaching, administration and/or scholarship appropriate to the programmatic need the individual is expected to fulfill. Areas of Departmental Need We expect the successful candidate(s) to develop or hold expertise in one or more of the following clinical and educational priorities. This list is not exhaustive and may evolve with departmental needs. We also welcome exploratory conversations about mutual fit and encourage interested candidates to apply. Access/Urgent Dermatologic Care Virtual Care Nail Disease Inpatient Consultative Dermatology High Risk Skin Cancer Supportive Dermato-Oncology Survivorship Qualifications MD or MD/PhD from an accredited medical school Board certification or board eligibility in dermatology Strong clinical dermatologic skills Commitment to trainee education Ability to work collaboratively in an academic medical center environment Applications will be reviewed beginning September 30, 2026 and accepted until January 31, 2027. Stanford is an equal employment opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Stanford welcomes applications from all who would bring additional dimensions to the University’s research, teaching and clinical missions. Consistent with its obligations under the law, the University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities. Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact disability.access@stanford.edu . The university’s central functions of research and education depend on freedom of thought, and expression. The Department of Dermatology, School of Medicine, and Stanford University value faculty who will help foster an open and respectful academic environment for colleagues, students, and staff with a wide range of backgrounds, identities, and perspectives. Candidates may choose to include as part of their research and teaching statements a brief discussion about how their work and experience will further these values. Apply at the link above with CV , a letter of interest, and the names of three references. For questions, please contact dermatologyfacultyaffairs@stanford.edu. The expected base pay range for this position is: Assistant Professor $232,000-$244,000 This pay range reflects base pay, which is based on faculty rank and years in rank. It does not include all components of the School of Medicine’s faculty compensation program or pay from participation in departmental incentive compensation programs. For more information about compensation and our wide-range of benefits , including housing assistance , please contact the hiring department. Stanford University has provided a pay range representing its good faith estimate of what the university reasonably expects to pay for the position upon hire. The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors including (but not limited to) the experience and qualifications of the selected candidate including equivalent years in rank, training, and field or discipline; internal equity; and external market pay for comparable jobs. Back to all jobs Apply Now First Name (required) dd50f7ca Last Name (required) d76fa633 Email (required) 74c9d4b8 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign up for job alerts Job Alert d5f66be3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. School School of Medicine School of Medicine Line CE - Clinician Educator CE - Clinician Educator Location Stanford University, California, United States Stanford University, California, United States First Name (required) ae0f1148 Last Name (required) 9828f412 Email (required) c67944ce Subscribe Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Get Help Questions about a job or your application? Find out how to request help Equal Opportunity Stanford is an equal employment opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Stanford welcomes applications from all who would bring additional dimensions to the University’s research, teaching and clinical missions. Consistent with its obligations under the law, the University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities. Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact disability.access@stanford.edu . Stanford University Stanford Home Maps & Directions Search Stanford Emergency Info Terms of Use Cookie Preferences Privacy Copyright Trademarks Non-Discrimination Accessibility © 2026 Stanford University. Stanford, California 94305. Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
