    "https://facultypositions.stanford.edu/jobs/senior-faculty-position-in-chemistry-open-area-stanford-university-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Senior Faculty Position in Chemistry (Open Area)",
      "description": "Senior Faculty Position in Chemistry (Open Area) - Stanford University, California, United States Stanford Faculty Positions Site navigation Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode Open Faculty Positions Senior Faculty Position in Chemistry (Open Area) Stanford University University Tenure Line Opening at: Aug 1 2026 - 9:00am PDT Closing at: Dec 31 2026 - 11:55pm PST Add to favorites View favorites The Department of Chemistry at Stanford University seeks applicants for a senior appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. The search is open to applicants in all areas of experimental and theoretical chemistry. Applicants must have demonstrated a commitment to effective teaching and mentoring and the ability to maintain a world-class research program. The successful candidate must have a Ph.D. in Chemistry or a related field and will be expected to teach and advise students at both the graduate and undergraduate levels. The term of appointment is expected to begin on September 1, 2027. Candidates should apply through Stanford Faculty Positions and submit a cover letter curriculum vitae (including a publication list) a summary of their research program (no more than three single-spaced pages) a teaching statement (no more than 1 single-spaced page) The salary range for this position is $159,907-$178,030 for the rank of Associate Professor and $188,500-$341,136 for the rank of Full Professor for the academic year 2026–2027. Stanford University has provided a pay range representing its good faith estimate of what the university reasonably expects to pay for the position upon hire. The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors including (but not limited to) the qualifications of the selected candidate, budget availability, and internal equity. Further information about Stanford’s Department of Chemistry may be found at the department website ( https://chemistry.stanford.edu ). Inquiries may be directed to Brittany Forniotis, Faculty Affairs Administrator, fornioti[@]stanford.edu Review of applications will begin on November 3, 2026; later applications may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. The application process will close on December 31, 2026. Stanford is an equal employment opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Stanford welcomes applications from all who would bring additional dimensions to the University’s research, teaching and clinical missions. Consistent with its obligations under the law, the University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities. Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact disability.access@stanford.edu. Back to all jobs Apply Now First Name (required) d1684b39 Last Name (required) 37e67656 Email (required) b30417bc Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 36e09e06 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. School School of Humanities & Sciences School of Humanities & Sciences Line University Tenure Line University Tenure Line Location Stanford University, California, United States Stanford University, California, United States First Name (required) 71dbd924 Last Name (required) add10e8a Email (required) 72178b97 Subscribe Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Get Help Questions about a job or your application? Find out how to request help Equal Opportunity Stanford is an equal employment opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Stanford welcomes applications from all who would bring additional dimensions to the University’s research, teaching and clinical missions. Consistent with its obligations under the law, the University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities. Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact disability.access@stanford.edu . Stanford University Stanford Home Maps & Directions Search Stanford Emergency Info Terms of Use Cookie Preferences Privacy Copyright Trademarks Non-Discrimination Accessibility © 2026 Stanford University. Stanford, California 94305. Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
