    "https://facultypositions.stanford.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-latin-american-literature-and-cultures-including-brazil-stanford-university-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Latin American Literature and Cultures, including Brazil",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Latin American Literature and Cultures, including Brazil - Stanford University, California, United States Stanford Faculty Positions Site navigation Applicant Login My Profile Kiosk mode Open Faculty Positions Assistant Professor of Latin American Literature and Cultures, including Brazil Stanford University University Tenure Line Opening at: Jul 28 2026 - 2:00pm PDT Closing at: Oct 23 2026 - 11:55pm PDT Add to favorites View favorites The Department of Iberian and Latin American Cultures (ILAC) at Stanford University invites applications for a tenure-line Assistant Professor in Latin American literature and cultures, including Brazil. We welcome applicants working in any period, genre, or critical approach, including but not limited to literary studies, cultural studies, film and media, and visual culture. In addition to English, native or near-native proficiency in Spanish and/or Portuguese is required. Native or near-native proficiency in both languages is strongly preferred. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching, advise doctoral students, and participate in the broader intellectual life of the department and the university. ILAC is a diverse and internationally oriented department; it is housed within the Division of Literatures, Cultures, and Languages and maintains strong ties to interdisciplinary programs across the humanities. Candidates are expected to have the Ph.D. in hand by the appointment start date (September 1, 2027). We seek candidates with a demonstrated record of or clear promise in research, strong teaching experience, and a commitment to graduate mentorship. The term of appointment is expected to begin on September 1, 2027. Candidates should apply through Stanford Faculty Positions and submit : a cover letter curriculum vitae (including a complete publication list) a combined research and teaching statement (no more than three single-spaced pages) two writing samples (8,000-10,000 words each), one in English, one in Spanish or Portuguese sample syllabus for an undergraduate survey course in literature three letters of recommendation The Department of Iberian and Latin American Cultures, School of Humanities & Sciences, and Stanford University value faculty who will help foster an open and respectful academic environment for colleagues, students, and staff with a wide range of backgrounds and perspectives. Candidates may choose to include as part of their research and teaching statements a brief discussion about how their work and experience will further these values. The salary range for this position is $115,133 – $135,388 for the academic year 2026-2027. Stanford University has provided a pay range representing its good faith estimate of what the university reasonably expects to pay for the position. The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors including (but not limited to) the qualifications of the selected candidate, budget availability, and internal equity. Further information about Stanford’s Department of Iberian and Latin American Cultures may be found at https://dlcl.stanford.edu/departments/iberian-and-latin-american-cultures Inquiries may be directed to Christine Onorato, Administrator, Faculty Affairs, conorato@stanford.edu The application submission deadline is October 23, 2026. Stanford is an equal employment opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Stanford welcomes applications from all who would bring additional dimensions to the University’s research, teaching and clinical missions. Consistent with its obligations under the law, the University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities. Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact disability.access@stanford.edu. Back to all jobs Apply Now First Name (required) ed3c951b Last Name (required) 9873b4e0 Email (required) a209c79a Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign up for job alerts Job Alert a468e273 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. School School of Humanities & Sciences School of Humanities & Sciences Line University Tenure Line University Tenure Line Location Stanford University, California, United States Stanford University, California, United States First Name (required) 7f8f8968 Last Name (required) 4dbe3d1e Email (required) 372846f1 Subscribe Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Get Help Questions about a job or your application? Find out how to request help Equal Opportunity Stanford is an equal employment opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Stanford welcomes applications from all who would bring additional dimensions to the University’s research, teaching and clinical missions. Consistent with its obligations under the law, the University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities. Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact disability.access@stanford.edu . Stanford University Stanford Home Maps & Directions Search Stanford Emergency Info Terms of Use Cookie Preferences Privacy Copyright Trademarks Non-Discrimination Accessibility © 2026 Stanford University. Stanford, California 94305. Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
